    {
      "sentence_id": 4,
      "text": "01. Pursuant to the direction of this Court given in order dated 12.12.2025, learned counsel for the petitioner has come forward with the affidavit, which is yet to be made part of the digital file but has come on the physical file.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 555,
      "end": 788,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "12.12.2025",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 621,
          "end": 631
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "text": "02. By reference to his father-Om Singh's recorded position in the revenue record as is borne out from the khasra-girdhwari of 2025 in relation to khasra No. 267 min of revenue estate Panchal,\nregarding which even the Mutation of Inheritance has come to be attested in favour of the petitioner, his sister and mother, the petitioner came forward with the institution of this writ petition being aggrieved that part of his ownership land comprised in khasra No. 267 min has been appropriated for the purpose of road construction from Dhanmasta to Jarnal by the Public Works (Roads & Buildings) Department, Batote, Division Ramban, without adopting due course of law, as a Manour Singh vs Ut Of J&K & Ors on 29 December, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/38078701/\n1 result whereof the petitioner has been deprived of his ownership property without any compensation for which the petitioner is now invoking the writ jurisdiction of this Court for a mandamus unto the writ-respondent Nos. 1, 5 and 6 for undertaking acquisition under the Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition, Rehabilitation and Resettlement Act,\n2013.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 790,
      "end": 1948,
